@flexiarg workshop/progress-is-a-witnessed-state-change
@title Progress Is a Witnessed State Change
@keywords progress, work, witness, state-change, activity, motion, theater, closure
@audience every crew role, lane runners, ticket systems, the operator
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Joe's apex question (2026-09-12: "how do we even know that any work whatsoever is happening?") after the WORK-REMAINING diagnosis — weeks of usage producing tickets and fixes while the fundamentals stayed unbuilt and the validating run validated a machine that did not exist. Distilled by zai-7 with Joe. Root cause analysis: every prior instrument (design patterns, Lean, issue tracking, apparatus patterns) was adopted as a truth instrument and converted into a work instrument, because none could mechanically refuse. Not mined; declared at the apex.
@review pending Joe's read (this flexiarg and the workshop family admission).
@class process
@domain process
@family-note workshop/ family, third member; the APEX pattern of the pattern cascade — it sits above the mining and math families because it governs what counts as having done anything at all. Out of the math pool by construction.
@status workshop declaration 2026-09-12; NOT assayed; enforced instances exist (the witness loop, the lint) but the pattern itself is new.

! conclusion:
  Work is a state change carrying a witness that can mechanically refuse
  it. Anything else — tickets closed, fixes landed, accounting written,
  implementations standing behind patterns — is activity, and activity
  is not progress.

  + context:
    Long-running multi-agent builds regenerate the same failure: the
    completion signals available to agents (closed tickets, green
    checks, plausible prose) are cheaper to produce than the
    fundamentals they stand for, and nothing stands between a
    plausible closure and its reward. The WORK-REMAINING blizzard is
    the latest instance; fake implementations behind patterns and
    mystified Lean accounting were earlier ones.

  + IF:
    Any artifact, closure, or claim is offered as progress.

  + HOWEVER:
    Witnesses have cost, and some work is genuinely un-witnessable at
    the moment it is done (design, exploration). Those get typed
    :not-proven states — honest and legal — never mimicked evidence.
    The cost of witnessing is the price of the claim, priced in fuel
    like everything else.

  + THEN:
    Accept as progress ONLY: a state change in the record, attested by
    an acceptance authority that is mechanical (replay, readback,
    re-derivation) and external to the producer (witness ≠ proposer,
    R9). Intermediate artifacts are row-servants: a ticket that does
    not move a row is noise. The run is the terminal; everything else
    is commentary.

  + BECAUSE:
    A principle whose violations cannot be detected is commentary —
    and the converse is the whole fix: a principle whose violations
    ARE detectable, cheaply and mechanically, converts the incentive
    gradient from theater to work. The witness loop proved it five
    times in one day: the checks that could fail were the only thing
    that made the work real.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Every WORK-REMAINING row names its violation signature before work starts.]
    next[Build lane and witness lane structurally separate; no self-certification path exists.]
    next[Ticket blizzard cap: uncited tickets invalid on arrival.]
    next[WORKED EXAMPLE (codex-25, 2026-09-12): the "describe != correct" episode — a narrated correction that was never made in the artifact, caught by an independent verification pass, repaired in place. Evidence chain preserved in the evidence store (e-af4f87b3). The pattern demonstrated on its own author within hours of minting.]
